 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [Regular Grid](3950-regular-grid.md)
-Uses a 1D array of linked lists for primitives. Conservative mapping ensures no primitive is missed. Handles intersections outside the current cell by continuing traversal.
+A spatial acceleration structure dividing an AABB into a fixed-size uniform 3D grid of cells(3950-regular-grid.md). Sets apart by partitioning space into disjoint sub-blocks where primitives can belong to multiple cells, unlike BVH which partitions primitives(3950-regular-grid.md). Choose for scenes with uniform data distribution on GPUs(3950-regular-grid.md).
 
 ### [Voxel-based Ray Tracing for GI and Specular Reflections](4091-voxel-based-ray-tracing-for-gi-and-specular-reflections.md)
-Uses a 128³ occupancy grid for GI/Reflection fallbacks. Integrates with Light Propagation Volumes (LPV) and requires `GL_ARB_shader_image_load_store`.
+A voxel-based ray tracing system using DDA through a 128³ block-occupancy grid for GI and specular reflection fallbacks(4091-voxel-based-ray-tracing-for-gi-and-specular-reflections.md). Sets apart by integrating with Light Propagation Volumes (LPV) and acting as a drop-in replacement for Screen-Space Ray Tracing(4091-voxel-based-ray-tracing-for-gi-and-specular-reflections.md). Choose when screen-space coverage is incomplete or for sky occlusion with LPV colour bleeding(4091-voxel-based-ray-tracing-for-gi-and-specular-reflections.md).
 
 ### [Optimised Voxel Ray Marching](4240-optimised-voxel-ray-marching.md)
-Uses bitwise operations for chunk indexing to minimize arithmetic overhead. Optimized for fixed-step traversal within working chunks.
+A fixed-step ray traversal algorithm for voxel-based scenes minimizing computational overhead by keeping block lookups within the current working chunk(4240-optimised-voxel-ray-marching.md). Sets apart by replacing global coordinate arithmetic with bitwise operations for chunk indexing(4240-optimised-voxel-ray-marching.md). Choose for hierarchical voxel maps where reducing bitshifts and multiplications per step is critical(4240-optimised-voxel-ray-marching.md).
 
 ## Background
-Regular grids are a foundational spatial acceleration structure in ray tracing [G]. They partition space into disjoint sub-blocks, unlike BVH which partitions primitives [Regular Grid](3950-regular-grid.md). Effective on GPUs due to spatial locality [Regular Grid](3950-regular-grid.md).
+Regular grids are a foundational spatial acceleration structure in ray tracing [G]. They partition space into disjoint sub-blocks, unlike BVH which partitions primitives [S2, S3, Regular Grid](3950-regular-grid.md). Effective on GPUs due to spatial locality [S3, Regular Grid](3950-regular-grid.md).
 
